WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.708 --> 00:00:06.130
My plan was to invent a relaxing bubble bath soap that would help Molly sleep.

2
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.971
Inventors call that "formulating."

3
00:00:08.991 --> 00:00:14.694
I had decided to formulate a special soap just for Molly.

4
00:00:30.008 --> 00:00:31.989
I couldn't wait to get started!

5
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:38.192
When we got home, Molly asked her babysitter if she could go to my apartment.

6
00:00:38.212 --> 00:00:44.694
"Okay," said Lucy, who was watching TV with Caswell in the living room.

7
00:00:44.714 --> 00:00:48.816
"You're missing a great episode of Monster Madness!"

8
00:00:49.476 --> 00:00:50.657
Caswell told Molly.

9
00:00:51.757 --> 00:00:57.400
Sure enough, I could hear the roars of monsters and the screams of frightened people coming from the

10
00:00:57.460 --> 00:01:04.666
TV. "Let's get out of here," Molly whispered to me.

11
00:01:06.087 --> 00:01:09.430
A few minutes later, Molly and I were sitting at my kitchen table.

12
00:01:10.531 --> 00:01:14.374
Molly looked a little better, but she still seemed pretty upset.

13
00:01:14.394 --> 00:01:18.997
"I'm going to formulate a very special invention," I told her.

14
00:01:19.017 --> 00:01:22.500
"It will help you relax so you can sleep better."

15
00:01:23.961 --> 00:01:27.624
"I hope it works," said Molly with a sigh.

16
00:01:28.864 --> 00:01:32.907
"As soon as I close my eyes at night, a scary monster appears in my mind!"

17
00:01:32.927 --> 00:01:37.210
"Don't worry," I said.

18
00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.331
"My invention will fix that.

19
00:01:39.571 --> 00:01:41.613
What's your favorite food in the whole world?"

20
00:01:42.934 --> 00:01:44.155
Molly's face brightened.

21
00:01:44.175 --> 00:01:46.496
"Cherries!" she said.

22
00:01:46.516 --> 00:01:48.437
"I love cherries!"

23
00:01:48.457 --> 00:01:57.684
"Okay." I went to the cupboard and rummaged around until I found a bottle of cherry juice.

24
00:01:58.856 --> 00:02:00.817
Molly was watching me with curiosity.

25
00:02:00.837 --> 00:02:04.079
"Are you going to make me something to drink?"

26
00:02:04.579 --> 00:02:05.159
she asked.

27
00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.641
"I'm going to make something even better than that!"

28
00:02:09.142 --> 00:02:09.782
I promised.

29
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:14.725
I got an empty jar and filled it up with soapy water.

30
00:02:18.367 --> 00:02:21.508
Then I poured lots of cherry juice into the jar.

31
00:02:22.489 --> 00:02:24.830
I shook up the mixture until it was all foamy.

32
00:02:25.951 --> 00:02:28.452
At last I handed it to Molly.

33
00:02:29.632 --> 00:02:30.252
"Here you go!"

34
00:02:30.673 --> 00:02:31.073
I said.

35
00:02:31.093 --> 00:02:35.555
"Your very own mixture of Enchanting Cherry bath soap.

36
00:02:36.935 --> 00:02:39.376
Pour it into the tub before you take a bath tonight.

37
00:02:40.297 --> 00:02:42.838
It will totally relax you before bedtime!"

38
00:02:42.858 --> 00:02:46.479
"Iggy!" yelled Tate from his room.

39
00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:49.201
"Get in here and get your stuff!"

40
00:02:50.621 --> 00:02:56.344
Boy, I couldn't wait until I formulated special bubble bath soaps so Tate could relax.

41
00:02:57.484 --> 00:02:59.606
But his favorite food is granola bars.

42
00:03:00.867 --> 00:03:03.328
Who wants to take a granola bar bath?

43
00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:09.313
I thought about Molly's Enchanting Cherry bubble bath all through dinner.

44
00:03:10.634 --> 00:03:14.157
I couldn't wait to hear about how my invention had helped her.

45
00:03:15.457 --> 00:03:19.841
I had just finished getting my stuff out of Tate's closet when the doorbell rang.

46
00:03:19.861 --> 00:03:22.943
"It's for you, Piggy!"

47
00:03:23.283 --> 00:03:23.924
Tate called.

48
00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:28.129
Sometimes my brother calls me "Piggy" instead of "Iggy."

49
00:03:29.329 --> 00:03:30.910
He does it just to get me mad.

50
00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:33.350
I didn't get mad this time though.

51
00:03:34.571 --> 00:03:39.012
After all, I'm the guy who invents things to calm people down, right?

52
00:03:40.172 --> 00:03:41.052
I went to the door.

53
00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:46.554
Molly was standing there in her bathrobe and slippers.

54
00:03:46.574 --> 00:03:49.795
"Iggy," she said, glaring at me.

55
00:03:49.815 --> 00:03:53.816
"I tried taking an Enchanting Cherry bubble bath!"

56
00:03:55.184 --> 00:03:56.145
"What's the matter?"

57
00:03:56.505 --> 00:03:56.986
I asked.

58
00:03:57.006 --> 00:03:59.928
"It was really sticky!"

59
00:04:00.349 --> 00:04:01.169
Molly cried.

60
00:04:01.189 --> 00:04:02.831
"And itchy!"

61
00:04:02.851 --> 00:04:08.215
"Uh-oh," I thought, watching her scratch her arms.

62
00:04:09.396 --> 00:04:14.600
I didn't want to say anything, but her skin looked a little red—as in cherry red.

63
00:04:15.541 --> 00:04:19.144
My brilliant invention had obviously backfired.

64
00:04:20.686 --> 00:04:23.228
Suddenly Molly gave me a pleading look.

65
00:04:24.492 --> 00:04:26.213
"You have to help me, Iggy.

66
00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.434
I don't want to think about monsters again tonight!"

67
00:04:30.874 --> 00:04:31.834
My heart sunk.

68
00:04:32.635 --> 00:04:35.755
I needed a new idea, and I needed it fast.

69
00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.617
Or poor Molly would never get any sleep.

70
00:04:40.637 --> 00:04:41.337
I could do it.

71
00:04:42.057 --> 00:04:42.878
I knew I could.

72
00:04:43.438 --> 00:04:49.380
After all, I was Iggy the incredible inventor, and my best friend was depending on me.
